hadiths[155]{hadithnumber,text}:
"639","Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him) reports that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) delivered a sermon to us and said: O people! Hajj has been made obligatory upon you, so perform Hajj. A man asked: O Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him)! Is it necessary (to perform Hajj) every year? The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) remained silent. The man repeated this question three times, so the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: If I had said yes, it would have become obligatory every year and you would not have been able to do it. So leave me with what I have left you with. Indeed, those before you were destroyed only because they asked too many questions of their prophets and differed with them excessively. So when I command you to do something, do as much of it as you can, and when I forbid you from something, then avoid it."
"640","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah, may Allah be pleased with him, that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, said: One ‘Umrah to the next ‘Umrah is an expiation for the sins committed between them, and the reward for an accepted Hajj is nothing except Paradise."
"641","Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him) reports that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: Whoever comes to this House (the Ka'bah) and does not engage in idle or lustful talk, nor commits any sin, returns as free from sins as the day his mother gave birth to him."
"642","‘Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that Sayyiduna Abu Bakr (may Allah be pleased with him), during the Hajj in which the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) appointed him as leader before the Farewell Hajj, sent me among the group who, on the Day of Sacrifice, proclaimed that after this year no polytheist would perform Hajj and no one would circumambulate the House naked (as was done in the days of ignorance). Ibn Shihab Zuhri (may Allah have mercy on him) said that Humaid, son of Abdur Rahman, also used to say, due to this very hadith of Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him), that the Day of Greater Hajj is indeed the Day of Sacrifice."
"643","Narrated from Umm al-Mu’minin Aisha Siddiqa (may Allah be pleased with her) that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: There is no day on which Allah frees more servants from the Fire than the Day of Arafah. And Allah draws near (to His servants) and boasts about them to the angels and says: What do these people want?"
"644","Narrated from Sayyiduna Ali Azdi (may Allah be pleased with him) that Sayyiduna Ibn Umar (may Allah be pleased with them both) taught him that when the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) would mount his camel to set out on a journey, he would say ""Allahu Akbar"" three times, then recite this supplication: ""Glory be to Him Who has subjected this (animal) to us, and we could never have subdued it, and surely to our Lord we are returning."" {Az-Zukhruf: 14,13} ""O Allah! We ask You for goodness and piety in this journey of ours, and for deeds that please You. O Allah! Make this journey easy for us and shorten its distance for us. O Allah! You are the Companion in the journey and the Guardian over the family. O Allah! I seek refuge with You from the hardships of travel, from having a change of heart and being in a bad predicament, and from an ill-fated return with regard to wealth and family."" (He would recite this when setting out) and when returning, he would recite the same supplication, but would add: ""We are returning, repenting, worshipping our Lord, and praising Him."
"645","Abu Sa'id Al-Khudri (may Allah be pleased with him) reports that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: It is not permissible for a woman who believes in Allah and the Last Day to travel for more than three days unless she is accompanied by her father, her son, her husband, her brother, or another relative with whom she cannot marry."
"646","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) that the Noble Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) forbade a woman from undertaking a journey of one day (alone) unless her husband or another mahram relative is with her."
"647","Narrated Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them) that I heard the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say in a sermon: ""No man should be alone with a woman except when her mahram is with her. And no woman should travel except with a mahram relative."" Then a man stood up and said, ""O Messenger of Allah! My wife has set out for Hajj and my name has been registered in such-and-such army (i.e., I have been enlisted among the warriors)."" The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said, ""Go and perform Hajj with your wife."
"648","Narrated by Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both) from the Noble Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) that some people riding camels met the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) at (the place) Rauha. The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) asked them, ""Who are you?"" They replied, ""We are Muslims."" Then those people asked the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him), ""Who are you?"" The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said, ""I am the Messenger of Allah."" Then a woman lifted a child with her hands and asked, ""Is there Hajj for this child?"" The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said, ""Yes, and you will have the reward (i.e., the parents)."
"649","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them) that he said: Sayyiduna Fadl bin Abbas (may Allah be pleased with him) was riding behind the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him). Then a woman from the tribe of Khath'am came and she began to ask the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) something, and Sayyiduna Fadl began to look at her, so she began to look at Fadl. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) turned Fadl's face to the other side. The woman said: O Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him)! Allah has made Hajj obligatory upon His servants, and my father is so old that he cannot sit on a mount. Should I perform Hajj on his behalf? The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: Yes. And this was during the Farewell Pilgrimage."
"650","‘Mother of the Believers, Aisha Siddiqa (may Allah be pleased with her) says that’ Asma bint Umais began experiencing postnatal bleeding due to the birth of Muhammad bin Abi Bakr during the journey at Dhul-Hulaifah, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) instructed Abu Bakr (may Allah be pleased with him) to tell her to perform ghusl (ritual bath) and recite the Talbiyah."
"651","`Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both) says that` the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) fixed Dhu’l-Hulayfah as the miqat for the people of Madinah, Juhfah for the people of Sham, Qarn al-Manazil for the people of Najd, and Yalamlam for the people of Yemen. And all these miqats are for those who live in these regions and also for those who come from other countries with the intention of Hajj or Umrah to those places. Then those who reside within these miqats, that is, those closer to Makkah, should enter ihram from where they are, so much so that the people of Makkah should call out the talbiyah from Makkah itself."
"652","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Abu Zubair that he heard from Sayyiduna Jabir bin Abdullah (may Allah be pleased with him) (when) he was asked about the place for putting on Ihram, so he said—and I think he narrated it as a marfu’ hadith—that I heard the Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) say: For the people of Madinah, the place for entering Ihram is Dhu’l-Hulaifah; for those coming by the other route, it is Juhfah; for the people of Iraq, the place for entering Ihram is Dhat ‘Irq; for the people of Najd, it is Qarn al-Manazil; and for the people of Yemen, it is Yalamlam."
"653","Umm al-Mu'mineen Aisha Siddiqa (may Allah be pleased with her) says: I applied perfume to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) for his Ihram, when he assumed Ihram (before assuming Ihram), and for his becoming lawful (halal) before the Tawaf al-Ifadah."
"654","Umm al-Mu'mineen Aisha Siddiqa (may Allah be pleased with her) says: It is as if I can see the shine of musk in the parting of the hair of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him), and he was in the state of Ihram at that time."
"655","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Abu Sa'id Khudri (may Allah be pleased with him) that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) mentioned a woman from the Children of Israel who had filled her ring with musk, and musk is a very fine fragrance."
"656","Nafi' says that whenever Sayyiduna Ibn Umar (may Allah be pleased with them both) used incense, he would use pure aloeswood (oud) with nothing else mixed in it, or he would use camphor incense and add aloeswood to it, and then he would say that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) also used to use fragrance in this manner."
"657","Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him) reports that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever is offered fragrant grass or a fragrant flower should not refuse it (i.e., should not decline to take it), because it carries no burden and its fragrance is pleasant."
"658","Salim bin Abdullah narrates that he heard from his father, Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (may Allah be pleased with them), who said: ""This Baida is the very place where you people attribute lies to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him), and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) did not recite the Talbiyah except near the mosque of Dhul-Hulaifah."
"659","´It is narrated from Sayyiduna Ubaid bin Juraij that` he said to Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (may Allah be pleased with them): O Abu Abdur Rahman! I have seen you doing four things which I have not seen any of your companions doing. He said: O son of Juraij! What are those things? He said: First, I see that you do not touch any of the corners of the Ka'bah during Tawaf except the two corners which are towards Yemen. Second, you wear Sabti (tanned leather) shoes. Third, you dye (your beard) with saffron or wars, etc. Fourth, when you were in Makkah, people would start reciting Talbiyah as soon as they saw the new moon, but you recited it on the eighth of Dhul-Hijjah. So Sayyiduna Abdullah (may Allah be pleased with him) replied: (Listen!) As for the corners, I have not seen the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) touching them except those which are towards Yemen. And as for the Sabti shoes, I have seen the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) wearing such shoes in which there was no hair, and he would perform ablution in them (i.e., after performing ablution, he would wear them on his wet feet), so I also like to wear them. As for the yellow color, I have seen the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) dyeing with it (i.e., his hair or his clothes), so I also like to dye with it. And as for the Talbiyah, I have not seen the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) reciting the Talbiyah except when his she-camel stood up with him mounted (i.e., near the mosque of Dhul-Hulaifah)."
"660","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Jabir (may Allah be pleased with him), he said: We came with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) in the state of Ihram for Hajj Mufrad (single Hajj). (Perhaps his and some of the companions’ Ihram was like this, while the Noble Prophet (peace be upon him) was Qarin [performing Hajj and Umrah together]). And Umm al-Mu’minin Aisha Siddiqa (may Allah be pleased with her) came in the state of Ihram for Umrah, until when they reached (the place) Sarif, Umm al-Mu’minin Aisha Siddiqa (may Allah be pleased with her) began menstruating. Then when we came to Makkah and performed Tawaf of the Ka’bah and Sa’i between Safa and Marwah, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) commanded us that whoever does not have a Hadi (sacrificial animal) should open his Ihram (i.e., become halal). So we said: What kind of halal? He (peace be upon him) said: Complete halal. So then we completely opened our Ihram. The narrator said: Then we had intercourse with our women, applied perfume, and wore clothes, and at that time there were four nights left between us and ‘Arafah. Then on the Day of Tarwiyah (i.e., the 8th of Dhul-Hijjah), we put on Ihram (for Hajj). Then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came to Umm al-Mu’minin Aisha Siddiqa (may Allah be pleased with her) and found her weeping, so he asked: What has happened to you? She said: I have begun menstruating, and the people have opened their Ihram, but I have neither been able to open my Ihram nor perform Tawaf, and now the people are going for Hajj. So the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: This is a thing that Allah has decreed for all the daughters of Adam. So perform ghusl (ritual bath) and put on Ihram for Hajj. So she did so and stood at the places of standing (i.e., the rites of Hajj), until when she became pure, she performed Tawaf of the House (Ka’bah) and Sa’i between Safa and Marwah. Then the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: You have become halal from both Hajj and Umrah. She said: O Messenger of Allah! I find in my heart that I did not perform Tawaf (i.e., Tawaf Qudum) until I had completed Hajj. So the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: O Abdur Rahman (may Allah be pleased with him) (son of Abu Bakr, may Allah be pleased with him)! Take her to Tan’eem and let her perform Umrah. This happened on the night when we were staying at Muhassab."
"661","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (may Allah be pleased with them both) that when the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) mounted his she-camel and it stood straight with him near the mosque of Dhul-Hulaifah, then the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) recited the Talbiyah, that is: ""Here I am, O Allah, here I am, here I am. You have no partner, here I am. Surely all praise and blessings are for You, the kingdom is Yours, and You have no partner."" He said that Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (may Allah be pleased with them both) used to say that this was the Talbiyah of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him). Nafi’ says that Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (may Allah be pleased with them both) used to add these words: ""Here I am (in Your service), here I am (in Your service), and all good fortune is from You, and all goodness is in Your hands. Here I am, and I turn to You alone, and all actions are for You."
"662","Sayyiduna Anas (may Allah be pleased with him) says that I heard the Noble Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) say that he entered into the state of Ihram for both Hajj and Umrah, and said: ""Labbayk Umratan wa Hajjan,"" meaning: (O Allah) I am present with the intention of Umrah and Hajj. I am present with the intention of Umrah and Hajj."
"663","Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates from the Noble Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) that he said: By Him in Whose hand is the life of Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him), the son of Mary (peace be upon him) will surely proclaim Talbiyah in the valley of ""Rawha"". He will either be performing Hajj, or Umrah, or both Hajj and Umrah together."
"664","´Sayyiduna Ibn Umar (may Allah be pleased with them both) says that` we proclaimed the Talbiyah for Hajj Mufrad with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him). In another narration, it is stated that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) proclaimed the Talbiyah for Hajj Mufrad."
"665","It is narrated from Ummul Momineen Aisha Siddiqa (may Allah be pleased with her) that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) performed Hajj Ifrad (that is, performed only Hajj)."
"666","Narrated from Sayyiduna Bakr bin Abdullah that Sayyiduna Anas (may Allah be pleased with him) said: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) reciting the Talbiyah for both Hajj and Umrah. Bakr said: I narrated this same hadith to Sayyiduna Ibn Umar (may Allah be pleased with them both), and he said: The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) recited the Talbiyah only for Hajj. So I met Sayyiduna Anas (may Allah be pleased with him) and told him that Sayyiduna Ibn Umar (may Allah be pleased with them both) says so. Sayyiduna Anas (may Allah be pleased with him) said: You people consider us children; I have heard very well that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) used to say: Labbaik for Umrah and Hajj."
"667","Sayyiduna Imran bin Husain (may Allah be pleased with him) says: We performed Hajj Tamattu‘ with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him), and nothing was revealed in the Qur’an about it (i.e., prohibiting it). Whatever a person said about it was from his own opinion. (The reference is to Sayyiduna Umar (may Allah be pleased with him), who used to prohibit Hajj Tamattu‘). { مقام غور ہے کہ سیدنا عمر رضی اللہ عنہ جیسے صحابی کی بات جب آپ صلی اللہ علیہ وسلم کی بات کے خلاف تھی تو صحابہ کرام نے سیدنا عمر رضی اللہ عنہ کی بات کا انکار کر دیا ، اور آج ہم اور ہمارے علماء ( منہ سے بھلے اقرار نہ کریں لیکن عملاً ) اماموں کی بات کی وجہ سے آپ صلی اللہ علیہ وسلم کی بات ( احادیث ) چھوڑ دیتے ہیں ۔ اللہ تعالیٰ ہم کو سیدھا رستہ دکھائے آمین }"
"668","`Sayyiduna Imran bin Husain (may Allah be pleased with him) said that` the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) performed Hajj Tamattu‘ and we also performed Hajj Tamattu‘ along with him."
"669","`Sayyiduna Jabir bin Abdullah (may Allah be pleased with him) says that` we came with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and we were reciting the Talbiyah for Hajj, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) commanded us to change this Ihram of Hajj into Ihram of Umrah."
"670","Musa bin Nafi’ says: I came to Makkah four days before the Day of Tarwiyah with the intention of benefiting from Hajj along with ‘Umrah (Hajj Tamattu’), so people said to me, “Your Hajj is like the Hajj of the people of Makkah.” Then I went to ‘Ata bin Abi Rabah and asked him about the issue, so ‘Ata said: Jabir bin ‘Abdullah (may Allah be pleased with him) narrated to me that he performed Hajj with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) in the year when he had the sacrificial animal with him (i.e., in the Farewell Hajj, because after migration, the Prophet performed only one Hajj), and some people had assumed Ihram only for Hajj Mufrad. So the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: “Open your Ihram, perform Tawaf of the House (Ka’bah), perform Sa’i between Safa and Marwah, shorten your hair, and become lawful (i.e., come out of Ihram), until when the Day of Tarwiyah comes (i.e., 8th Dhul-Hijjah), then proclaim the Talbiyah for Hajj, and make the Ihram you brought with you as Hajj Tamattu’ (i.e., even if it was Ihram for Hajj, perform ‘Umrah, come out of Ihram, and then perform Hajj, so it will become Hajj Tamattu’).” The people said, “How can we make it Tamattu’ when we have named it Hajj?” The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: “Do as I command you. For if I had not brought the sacrificial animal with me, I would have done as I am commanding you, but my Ihram cannot be opened until the sacrifice reaches its place (i.e., the place of slaughter).” Then the people did as the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) had commanded."
"671","´Sayyiduna Abu Musa (may Allah be pleased with him) says that` I came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him), and he had made his camels kneel on the stony ground of Makkah (that is, he had encamped there). The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) asked me, ""With what intention have you put on Ihram?"" I replied, ""With the same intention as the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) has put on Ihram."" The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) asked, ""Have you brought a sacrificial animal with you?"" I said, ""No."" So the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said, ""Perform the Tawaf of the House of Allah and the Sa'i between Safa and Marwah, then come out of Ihram."" So I performed the Tawaf of the House of Allah and the Sa'i between Safa and Marwah, then I went to a woman from my people (she was my mahram), and she combed my hair and washed my head. Then, during the caliphate of Abu Bakr and Umar (may Allah be pleased with them both), I began giving people the same fatwa (that is, whoever comes for Hajj without a sacrificial animal should come out of Ihram after performing Umrah, then on the Day of Tarwiyah, the 8th of Dhul-Hijjah, put on Ihram again for Hajj). But once, while I was standing at the place of Hajj, suddenly a man came and said, ""(You give the fatwa to come out of Ihram), do you know that the Commander of the Faithful, Sayyiduna Umar (may Allah be pleased with him), has started a new practice regarding the sacrificial animal?"" (That is, Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) said that after performing Umrah, one should not come out of Ihram.) So I said, ""O people! Whoever we have given this fatwa to, he should stop. Because the Commander of the Faithful, Sayyiduna Umar (may Allah be pleased with him), is coming, so follow him."" When Sayyiduna Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) arrived, I said, ""O Commander of the Faithful, what is this new ruling you have given regarding the sacrificial animal?"" Sayyiduna Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) replied, ""If you act upon the Book of Allah, the Qur'an says: ((Wa atimmu al-hajja wal-umrata lillah)) — that is, complete Hajj and Umrah for Allah (meaning, do not come out of Ihram), and if you act upon the Sunnah of the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him), his own practice was that he did not come out of Ihram until he had offered the sacrifice."
"672","‘Sayyiduna Abu Dharr (may Allah be pleased with him) says that’ Hajj Tamattu‘ was specific for the companions of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). (This is the statement of Sayyiduna Abu Dharr (may Allah be pleased with him), not a hadith of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him))."
"673","Narrated from Nafi‘ that Abdullah bin Umar (may Allah be pleased with them both) set out for ‘Umrah during the days of tribulation and said: If I am prevented from reaching the House of Allah, I will do as we did with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him). Then he assumed the Ihram for ‘Umrah and set out until he reached (the place) Bida’, (where most of the Companions heard the Talbiyah of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) during the Farewell Hajj). He said to his companions: The ruling of Hajj and ‘Umrah is the same, that both can be entered into with Ihram. So I make you witnesses that I have made Hajj obligatory upon myself along with ‘Umrah. Then he proceeded until he reached the House of Allah, performed seven circuits of Tawaf, and made Sa‘i between Safa and Marwah seven times. He did nothing more than this and considered it sufficient, and he offered a sacrifice."
"674","Salim bin Abdullah narrates that Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (may Allah be pleased with them both) says that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) performed Hajj Tamattu’ in the Farewell Hajj by combining Umrah with Hajj, and he offered a sacrifice, and he had brought the sacrificial animals with him from Dhu’l-Hulayfah. In the beginning, he proclaimed the Talbiyah for Umrah, then proclaimed the Talbiyah for Hajj, and likewise, the people also benefited from combining Umrah with Hajj along with him. Among the people, some had sacrificial animals with them, and some did not. Then, when the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) reached Makkah, he said to the people: Whoever has brought a sacrificial animal with him, he should not make anything lawful for himself from those things which are forbidden due to Ihram until he completes the Hajj. And whoever has not brought a sacrificial animal, he should perform Tawaf of the House of Allah, and Sa’i between Safa and Marwah, then cut his hair and come out of Ihram. Then (on the eighth of Dhu’l-Hijjah) he should proclaim the Talbiyah for Hajj, and after Hajj, he should offer a sacrifice, and whoever cannot find a sacrifice, he should fast three days during Hajj and seven days when he returns home. And when the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) came to Makkah, he first kissed the Black Stone, then ran for three circuits out of seven (which is called Raml), and walked for four circuits (as is customary). Then, when he finished the Tawaf, he performed two rak’ahs at the Station of Ibrahim. Then he completed the prayer and sat on Safa, and performed Sa’i seven times between Safa and Marwah. Then he did not make anything lawful for himself from those things which were forbidden due to Ihram until he had completely finished the Hajj, and he slaughtered his sacrifice on the Day of Sacrifice, i.e., the tenth of Dhu’l-Hijjah, and after coming to Makkah, he performed the Tawaf of Ifadah of the House of Allah. Then he made everything lawful for himself which had been forbidden in Ihram. And those people who had brought sacrificial animals with them did exactly as the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) had done."
"675","Narrated from Umm al-Mu’minin Aisha Siddiqa (may Allah be pleased with her) that she said: We set out with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) for the Farewell Pilgrimage, and some of us entered into ihram for ‘Umrah and some for Hajj. When we reached Makkah, the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Whoever has entered into ihram for ‘Umrah and has not brought a sacrificial animal, let him exit ihram; and whoever has entered into ihram for ‘Umrah and has brought a sacrificial animal, let him not exit ihram until he has slaughtered his sacrifice; and whoever has entered into ihram for Hajj, let him complete his Hajj. Umm al-Mu’minin Aisha Siddiqa (may Allah be pleased with her) said: I began menstruating and remained in that state until the Day of ‘Arafah, and I had only entered into ihram for ‘Umrah. So the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) instructed me to abandon the ‘Umrah and enter into ihram for Hajj. She said: So I did so. When the Hajj was completed, he sent with me ‘Abdur Rahman (bin Abi Bakr, may Allah be pleased with him) so that I could go to Tan‘im and perform ‘Umrah (by entering into ihram), the ‘Umrah which I had not completed and for which I had entered into ihram before entering into ihram for Hajj."
"676","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both) that Duba’ah (may Allah be pleased with her), daughter of Zubair bin Abdul Muttalib, came to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) and said: “I am a heavy, burdened woman and I intend to perform Hajj, so what do you command me?” The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: “Enter into the state of Ihram for Hajj and stipulate the condition that: ‘O Allah! My place of exiting Ihram will be where You restrain me.’” (The narrator of the hadith, Ibn Abbas, may Allah be pleased with them both, said:) She was able to complete the Hajj (and did not need to exit Ihram early)."
"677","Ya’la ibn Umayyah (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates from his father that a man came to the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) while he was at Ji’ranah, and that man was wearing a cloak on which there was some perfume, or he said there was some yellowish tint. He asked, “O Messenger of Allah, what do you command me regarding the (method of) ‘Umrah?” Meanwhile, revelation began to descend upon the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him), so a cloth was placed over him. Ya’la (may Allah be pleased with him) says, “I wished that I could see the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) at the time when revelation descended upon him.” Then he says that Sayyiduna ‘Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) said, “Do you wish to see the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) while revelation is descending upon him?” Then Sayyiduna ‘Umar (may Allah be pleased with him) lifted the corner of the cloth, and I saw the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) panting and snoring. The narrator said, “I think he said, ‘like a young camel pants.’” Then, when the revelation was complete, the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said, “Where is the questioner who was asking about ‘Umrah?” (And he said,) “Wash off the yellowish tint or,” he said, “the effect of perfume, etc., from your clothes, and take off your shirt, and do in ‘Umrah what you do in Hajj.”"
"678","Narrated from Sayyiduna Ibn Umar (may Allah be pleased with them both) that a man asked the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him): ""Which kinds of clothes may a Muhrim wear?"" The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) replied: ""Do not wear shirts, nor turbans, nor trousers, nor cloaks, nor socks, except if someone cannot find sandals, then let him wear socks after cutting them below the ankles. And do not wear any garment that has been touched with saffron or dyed with 'wars'."
"679","`Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them) says that` I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) delivering a sermon, and he (peace be upon him) said: The trousers are for the (Muhrim) who does not find an izar (waist-wrapper), and the leather socks are for the (Muhrim) who does not find sandals."
"680","Narrated from Sayyiduna Sa'b bin Jaththamah al-Laithi (may Allah be pleased with him) that he presented the meat of a wild donkey as a gift to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) while he (the Prophet) was at (the place of) Abwa or Dhuwan, so the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) returned it. He says: When the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) saw sadness on my face, he said: We did not return it for any other reason, except that we are in the state of Ihram."
"681","Tawoos narrates from Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both) that Zaid bin Arqam (may Allah be pleased with him) came, so Sayyiduna Abdullah (may Allah be pleased with him) reminded him and said: How did you report about the meat of the game that was gifted to the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) while he was in the state of Ihram? He said: A portion of the meat of the game was gifted to the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him), so he returned it and said: We are in the state of Ihram, so we do not eat it."
"682","´Sayyiduna Abu Qatadah (may Allah be pleased with him) says that` the Noble Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) set out for Hajj and we were with him. Sayyiduna Abu Qatadah (may Allah be pleased with him) said that the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) told some of his companions, among whom was Abu Qatadah, ""You take the route along the seashore until you meet me."" Then those people took the route along the seashore. Then, when they turned towards the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him), all of them entered into the state of Ihram except Sayyiduna Abu Qatadah (may Allah be pleased with him), who did not enter into Ihram. In short, as they were traveling on the way, they saw some wild donkeys, and Sayyiduna Abu Qatadah (may Allah be pleased with him) attacked them and cut the shanks of one of the donkeys. Then all his companions dismounted and ate its meat. Sayyiduna Abu Qatadah (may Allah be pleased with him) says that we ate the (hunted) meat while we were in the state of Ihram. He says, then we took the remaining meat with us, and when we reached the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him), we submitted, ""O Messenger of Allah! We had entered into Ihram, and Abu Qatadah (may Allah be pleased with him) had not entered into Ihram. Then we saw some wild donkeys, and Abu Qatadah attacked them and cut the shanks of one of them, so we dismounted and all of us ate its meat. Then we thought that we are eating the meat of hunted game while we are in Ihram? So we have brought the remaining meat with us."" Then the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said, ""Did any of you order him to do so or point towards it?"" Abu Qatadah says! So they replied, ""No."" The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said, ""Then eat the remaining meat (and there is no harm in it)."
"683","Umm al-Mu'minin Aisha Siddiqa (may Allah be pleased with her) narrates from the Noble Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) that he said: ""There are five harmful animals that may be killed both inside and outside the boundaries of the Haram. These include the snake, the speckled crow, the mouse, the rabid dog, and the kite."
"684","Narrated by Sayyiduna Ibn Umar (may Allah be pleased with them both) from the Noble Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) that he said: There are five animals for which there is no sin upon the one who kills them in the Haram and in the state of Ihram. These animals are: 1. Rat. 2. Scorpion. 3. Crow. 4. Kite. 5. Mad dog."
"685","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Ibn Buhaina (may Allah be pleased with him) that the Noble Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) had cupping done on the middle part of his head on the way to Makkah, and he (peace be upon him) was in the state of Ihram."
"686","Nabiyah bin Wahb says: We set out with Aban bin Uthman, and when we reached (the place) Milal (which is twenty-eight miles from Madinah on the way to Makkah), Umar bin Ubaidullah’s eyes began to hurt. And when we reached Rauha (a place), and the pain became severe, he sent a man to Aban bin Uthman to ask (about treatment). He said: Apply aloes (aloevera), because Sayyiduna Uthman (may Allah be pleased with him) narrated from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) that he said: When a man’s eyes begin to hurt and he is in the state of ihram, he should apply aloes to them."
"687","‘Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Haneen narrated from Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Abbas and Miswar bin Makhramah (may Allah be pleased with them) that’ there was a dispute between them at (the place of) Abwa. (About this matter that) Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both) said that a Muhrim can wash his head, and Sayyiduna Miswar (may Allah be pleased with him) said that he cannot (wash it). So Abdullah bin Haneen said that Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both) sent me to Sayyiduna Abu Ayyub (may Allah be pleased with him) to ask him about this. I found him bathing between two wooden poles of a well, and he was behind a cloth screen. I greeted him with salam, and he asked, “Who is it?” I said, “I am Abdullah bin Haneen, and Abdullah bin Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both) has sent me to you to ask how the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) used to wash his head while in Ihram.” So Sayyiduna Abu Ayyub (may Allah be pleased with him) placed both his hands on the cloth and lowered it a little until I could see his head. And he instructed the man who was pouring water over his head to pour water, so he poured water over him (his head). Then he would move his head and rub it forward and backward with his hands. Then he said, “I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) wash (his head) in this manner.”"
"688","Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Ma’qil says: I was sitting with Sayyiduna Ka’b (may Allah be pleased with him) in the mosque. I asked him about this verse: (So its compensation is fasting or charity or sacrifice) __QUR_N__. Sayyiduna Ka’b (may Allah be pleased with him) said: This was revealed about me. (Then he narrated the whole incident that) I had pain in my head, so I was taken to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) in such a condition that lice were falling from my head onto my face. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: I did not even imagine that you would be in so much pain. Well! Do you have a goat? I said: No. Then this verse was revealed: (So its compensation is fasting or charity or sacrifice) __QUR_N__ (i.e., during Hajj, do not shave your head while in the state of Ihram until you have offered a sacrifice, but if someone has pain in his head, he may shave his head, but he must pay a penalty: either fast, give charity, or offer a sacrifice). The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Either you will have to fast for three days, or feed six needy people, or give half a sa’ (i.e., about one and a quarter kilograms of food) of wheat or the like to each of six needy people. And (Ka’b, may Allah be pleased with him) said: This verse, in terms of its revelation, is specific to me, but in terms of practice, it is general for all people."
"689","Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both) narrates from the Noble Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) that a man fell from his camel and his neck broke, causing his death. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Bathe him with water and lote tree leaves, and shroud him in his two garments (i.e., the sheets of Ihram), and do not cover his head, for Allah will raise him on the Day of Resurrection reciting the Talbiyah."
"690","Nafi' says that Ibn Umar (may Allah be pleased with them) used to spend the night at Dhi Tuwa when going to Mecca, then perform ghusl (ritual bath) in the morning, and then enter Mecca during the day, and he used to mention that the Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) did the same."
"691","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Ibn Umar (may Allah be pleased with them both) that when the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) would leave (from Madinah), he would leave by the route of Shajarah and enter by the route of Mu’arras (Mu’arras is a place six miles from Madinah), and when he would enter Makkah, he would enter from the upper hill and when he would leave, he would leave from the lower hill."
"692","Narrated from Sayyiduna Usama bin Zaid bin Harithah (may Allah be pleased with him) that he said: O Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)! Will you reside in your house in Makkah? The Noble Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) replied: Has Aqeel left any house or wall for us? (that we would reside there) Because the heirs of Abu Talib were Aqeel and Talib, and Sayyiduna Ali (may Allah be pleased with him) and Sayyiduna Ja'far (may Allah be pleased with him) did not inherit anything. Because both of them had become Muslims, and Aqeel and Talib had not become Muslims. (For this reason, a Muslim and a disbeliever cannot inherit from each other.)"
"693","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Ibn Umar (may Allah be pleased with them both) that when the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) performed the initial Tawaf during Hajj or Umrah, he would jog three times, then walk four times, then offer two units of prayer, and then perform Sa’i between Safa and Marwah."
"694","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Jabir bin Abdullah (may Allah be pleased with him) that he said: I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) performing tawaf from the Black Stone to the Black Stone, jogging in three circuits."
"695","Sayyiduna Abu Tufail says: I said to Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them), ""What is your opinion regarding performing raml (brisk walk) three times and walking four times during tawaf? Because your people say that it is Sunnah."" He replied, ""They are both truthful and untruthful."" I asked, ""What does it mean that they spoke the truth and also lied?"" He said, ""When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) came to Makkah, the polytheists said that Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) and his companions cannot perform tawaf of the Sacred House due to weakness and frailty, and they were jealous of him. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) ordered that three rounds be done with raml and four rounds be walked as usual. (The point is, their falsehood was in considering this act as an intended, emphasized Sunnah, while the rest of the statement was true.) Then I said, 'Tell us about performing sa'i between Safa and Marwah while riding— is this Sunnah? Because your people call it Sunnah.' He said, 'They are both truthful and untruthful.' I asked, 'What does that mean?' He replied, 'When the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) came to Makkah, there was such a crowd of people that even virgin girls came out, and people began to say, ""This is Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him), this is Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him)."" And the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) was so good-natured that people would not be pushed away in front of him (meaning, there was no ""make way"" as is done for worldly rulers). Then, when the crowd became very large, the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) rode (an animal), and performing sa'i on foot is superior. (That is, the falsehood was in considering something done out of necessity as Sunnah without necessity, while the truth is that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) did perform sa'i while riding.)"
"696","‘Abdullah bin Sarjis says: I saw the bald one (that is, the one who has no hair on his head, meaning Sayyiduna ‘Umar, may Allah be pleased with him), and he was kissing the Black Stone while saying: “By Allah, I am kissing you and I know that you are a stone, you can neither harm nor benefit. And if I had not seen the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) kissing you, I would never have kissed you.” (From this statement, the idolaters, grave-worshippers, and those who seek intercession from graves are refuted, who kiss graves and such things thinking they will fulfill their wishes, because even the kissing of the Black Stone, which is the right hand of Allah, is only due to following the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), not because it can harm or benefit. So how can it be permissible to kiss other things, for which kissing is not established, rather it is prohibited, and that too with such impure beliefs?)"
"697","`Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (may Allah be pleased with them both) says that` ever since I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) touching the Hajar Aswad and the Yemeni Corner, I have never abandoned (touching them) — neither in hardship nor in ease (that is, no matter how much crowd there is, I do not leave touching them)."
"698","`Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both) says that` I did not see the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) performing istilam (touching or kissing) of any of the two Yemeni corners (Hajar Aswad and Rukn Yamani) except these two. (That is, he did not perform istilam of the other two corners.)"
"699","Sayyiduna Jabir (may Allah be pleased with him) reports that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) performed the Tawaf of the House of Allah during the Farewell Pilgrimage on his camel, and he would touch the Black Stone with his staff. (He rode) so that people could see him and he would be elevated, and so that they could ask him questions about religious matters, because the people had surrounded him in great numbers."
"700","‘It is narrated from Umm al-Mu’minin Umm Salamah (may Allah be pleased with her) that she complained to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) about her illness, so he (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: “Perform Tawaf riding behind all the people.” So she said: “I used to perform Tawaf while the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) was praying on one side of the House of Allah, in which he was reciting Surah at-Tur.”"
"701","‘Urwah says: I said to Umm al-Mu’minin ‘A’ishah Siddiqah (may Allah be pleased with her) that if I do not perform the Sa’i between Safa and Marwah, I think there is no harm. She asked: Why? ‘Urwah said: Because Allah Almighty says: “Indeed, Safa and Marwah are among the symbols of Allah. So whoever performs Hajj or ‘Umrah to the House, there is no blame upon him for walking between them.” { البقرہ : 158 } Umm al-Mu’minin (may Allah be pleased with her) said: If that were the case, Allah Almighty would have said: If anyone does not perform the Tawaf, there is no blame. And this verse was revealed about the people of the Ansar, for when they used to recite the Talbiyah in the time of ignorance, they would do so in the name of Manat and say: It is not right for us to perform Sa’i between Safa and Marwah. Then when they came for Hajj with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him), they mentioned this matter, so Allah Almighty revealed this verse. So, by my life, the Hajj of the one who does not perform the Sa’i between Safa and Marwah will not be complete. In another narration, Umm al-Mu’minin ‘A’ishah Siddiqah (may Allah be pleased with her) said: No one’s Hajj or ‘Umrah is complete until he performs the Tawaf (i.e., Sa’i) between Safa and Marwah."
"702","Sayyiduna Jabir bin Abdullah (may Allah be pleased with him) says that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and his companions performed Sa’i between Safa and Marwah only once. (That is, immediately after entering Makkah, after the Tawaf. Then, at the time of Tawaf Ifadah, it was not performed.)"
"703","‘Wabrah (that is, Ibn Abdur Rahman) says: I was sitting with Sayyiduna Ibn Umar (may Allah be pleased with them both) when a man came to him and said, “Is it correct to perform Tawaf before going to Arafat?” Sayyiduna Ibn Umar (may Allah be pleased with them both) said, “Yes.” So he said, “But Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both) says not to perform Tawaf before going to Arafat.” Sayyiduna Ibn Umar (may Allah be pleased with them both) said, “The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) performed Hajj and performed Tawaf of the House before going to Arafat. So if you are true (in your faith), is it better to take the statement of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) or that of Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both)?” It is a lesson that when the statement of a great jurist Companion like Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas is contrary to the statement of the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him), then even looking towards his statement is not permitted, let alone, as is common today, considering the statements of Imams or spiritual guides as religion without question. In another narration, Sayyiduna Ibn Umar (may Allah be pleased with them both) said: We saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) that he entered into Ihram for Hajj and performed Tawaf of the House and performed Sa’i between Safa and Marwah."
"704","'Amr bin Dinar said: We asked Ibn Umar (may Allah be pleased with them) whether a person who comes for Umrah and, after performing Tawaf of the Ka'bah, can have intercourse with his wife before performing Sa'i between Safa and Marwah? He replied: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) came to Makkah, performed Tawaf of the Ka'bah in seven circuits, prayed two rak'ahs behind Maqam Ibrahim, and performed Sa'i between Safa and Marwah seven times. And for you, the life of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) is a beautiful example."
"705","‘Sayyiduna Ibn Umar (may Allah be pleased with them both) narrates that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) came on the day of the conquest of Makkah and alighted in the courtyard of the Ka‘bah. He sent for ‘Uthman bin Talhah (may Allah be pleased with him), the keeper of the Ka‘bah’s key, so he brought the key and opened the door. The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him), Sayyiduna Bilal, Sayyiduna Usama, and ‘Uthman bin Talhah (may Allah be pleased with them) entered inside, and he ordered the door to be closed, so it was closed. (The Prophet and the companions) stayed for a short while, then the door was opened. I was the first of the people to meet the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) outside the Ka‘bah, and Sayyiduna Bilal (may Allah be pleased with him) was behind him. So I asked Sayyiduna Bilal (may Allah be pleased with him), “Did the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) pray?” He said, “Yes.” I asked, “Where?” He said, “Between the two pillars in front of him.” And I forgot to ask how many rak‘ahs he prayed."
"706","Ibn Jurayj says: I asked Ata, ""Have you heard Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both) say that you have been commanded to perform Tawaf, but not commanded to enter the Ka'bah?"" Ata said: ""He does not prohibit entering it, but I heard him say: Usama bin Zaid (may Allah be pleased with him) informed me that when the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) entered the Ka'bah, he supplicated in every direction and did not pray inside. Then when he came out, he prayed two rak'ahs in front of the Qiblah and said: 'This is the Qiblah.' I asked him: 'What is the ruling about its sides and what is the ruling about praying in its corners?' He said: 'Every side of the Sacred House is Qiblah.'"
"707","Ja'far bin Muhammad narrates from his father that: We went to the house of Sayyiduna Jabir bin Abdullah (may Allah be pleased with him), and he asked about everyone’s condition until when my turn came, I said, “I am Muhammad bin Ali, the grandson of Sayyiduna Husayn (may Allah be pleased with him).” So he stretched his hand towards me (with affection), placed his hand on my head, opened the top button of my shirt, then the lower button (i.e., of the shirt, etc.), and then placed his palm on my chest between my two breasts. I was a young boy at that time. Then he said, “Well done, welcome, O my nephew! Ask me whatever you wish.” Then I asked him, and he was not blind. Meanwhile, the time for prayer came, so he stood up wearing a sheet, and when he placed both its ends on his shoulders, due to the sheet being small, it would fall down, and his large sheet was placed on a side table. Then he led us in prayer (i.e., as imam). Then I said, “Inform me about the Hajj of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) (i.e., the Farewell Hajj).” So Sayyiduna Jabir (may Allah be pleased with him) gestured with his hand showing nine (9) and said, “The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) stayed in Madinah for nine years and did not perform Hajj. Then, in the tenth year, it was announced among the people that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) was going for Hajj. So many people gathered in Madinah, and all wanted to follow the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) and do as he did (in performing Hajj). Thus, we all set out with him until we reached Dhul-Hulaifah, where Asma bint Umais (may Allah be pleased with her) gave birth to Muhammad bin Abi Bakr (may Allah be pleased with him). She sent word to the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) asking what she should do (in the state of postnatal bleeding). He (peace and blessings be upon him) said, ‘Take a bath, tie a cloth around yourself, and enter into Ihram.’ Then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) prayed two rak’ahs in the mosque and mounted his she-camel Qaswa. When it took him straight to (the place) Baida, I looked ahead and saw as far as my eyes could see, there were riders and pedestrians, and on my right, left, and behind, there was a similar crowd of people, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) was among us, and the Qur’an was being revealed to him, and he knew its true meaning best. Whatever he did, we did the same. Then he proclaimed the Talbiyah with Tawheed, and the people also proclaimed the same Talbiyah as people do now (i.e., some people added words to the Talbiyah of the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him), and he did not stop them), and he continued to recite the Talbiyah. Sayyiduna Jabir (may Allah be pleased with him) said, ‘We intended nothing but Hajj and did not even recognize ‘Umrah, and to perform ‘Umrah during the days of Hajj was considered bad from the days of ignorance, until when we came to the House of Allah with him, he touched the Rukn (i.e., Hajar al-Aswad) and performed three circuits of Tawaf with Raml (i.e., walking briskly with small steps and swinging the shoulders), and four circuits walking normally. Then he came to Maqam Ibrahim and recited this verse: “Take the Maqam Ibrahim as a place of prayer,” and placed Maqam Ibrahim between himself and the House. Then my father used to say—and I do not know if he mentioned it from himself or from the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him)—that he (peace and blessings be upon him) prayed two rak’ahs and recited Surah Ikhlas and Surah Kafiroon in them. Then he returned to Hajar al-Aswad and kissed it, and exited from the door that leads to Safa. When he approached Safa (Safa is the name of a hill about twenty-five steps from the door of the Ka’bah), he recited this verse: “Indeed, Safa and Marwah are among the symbols of Allah,” and he (peace and blessings be upon him) said, “We begin with what Allah began with.” Then he (peace and blessings be upon him) ascended Safa until he saw the House of Allah, faced the Qiblah, and proclaimed the Oneness and greatness of Allah (i.e., said La ilaha illallah and Allahu Akbar), and said, “There is no deity worthy of worship except Allah alone, He fulfilled His promise (i.e., of spreading the religion and helping His Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him)), and He helped His servant (Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him)), and He alone defeated all the armies.” Then after that, he supplicated, then said the same, then supplicated. Thus, he did this three times. Then he descended and walked towards Marwah, and when his feet reached the middle of the valley, he ran until he reached Marwah. On Marwah, he did as he had done on Safa, i.e., said those words and supplicated facing the Qiblah. When the last circuit on Marwah was completed (i.e., seven circuits were done), he (peace and blessings be upon him) said, “If I had known beforehand what I came to know later, I would not have brought the sacrificial animal with me (and would have bought it in Makkah), and I would have made my Ihram for Hajj into ‘Umrah. So, whoever among you does not have a sacrificial animal with him, let him exit Ihram (i.e., after Tawaf and Sa’i, the acts of ‘Umrah are complete) and make it ‘Umrah.” (Upon hearing this) Suraqah bin Ju’sham stood up and said, “O Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him)! Is this making Hajj into ‘Umrah specific to this year or is it forever?” He (peace and blessings be upon him) interlaced the fingers of one hand into the other and said twice, “It is forever, forever.” Sayyiduna Ali (may Allah be pleased with him) came from Yemen with the camels of the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) and saw Sayyidah Fatimah (may Allah be pleased with her) among those who had exited Ihram, wearing colored clothes and with kohl in her eyes. Sayyiduna Ali (may Allah be pleased with him) disliked this, so she said, “My father ordered me to do so.” The narrator said that Sayyiduna Ali (may Allah be pleased with him) used to say in Iraq that I went to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) angry with Sayyidah Fatimah (may Allah be pleased with her) for exiting Ihram, and I informed him that I disliked it. He (peace and blessings be upon him) said, “Fatimah (may Allah be pleased with her) has spoken the truth (i.e., I ordered her to exit Ihram).” Then he (peace and blessings be upon him) said, “What intention did you make when you entered Ihram for Hajj?” I said, “I said, ‘O Allah! I enter into Ihram for whatever Your Messenger (peace and blessings be upon him) entered into Ihram for.’” He (peace and blessings be upon him) said, “I have the sacrificial animal with me (so I did not exit Ihram), so you also do not exit Ihram.” Sayyiduna Jabir (may Allah be pleased with him) said, “Then the camels that Sayyiduna Ali (may Allah be pleased with him) brought from Yemen and those that the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) brought with him together made one hundred camels.” Sayyiduna Jabir (may Allah be pleased with him) said, “Then all the people exited Ihram and trimmed their hair, except the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) and those who had the sacrificial animals with them (they remained in Ihram). When the Day of Tarwiyah came (i.e., the 8th of Dhul-Hijjah), all the people went to Mina and proclaimed the Talbiyah for Hajj, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) also rode and prayed Zuhr, Asr, Maghrib, Isha, and Fajr (five prayers) in Mina. Then he stayed there for a while until the sun rose, and he (peace and blessings be upon him) ordered that a tent made of hair be set up at (the place of) Namirah. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) set out, and the Quraysh believed that he (peace and blessings be upon him) would stop at al-Mash’ar al-Haram as was the custom of the Quraysh in the days of ignorance. He (peace and blessings be upon him) went ahead from there until he reached Arafat and found his tent set up at Namirah, so he entered it. When the sun had declined, Qaswa, his she-camel, was prepared at his command, and he (peace and blessings be upon him) came to the middle of the valley and delivered a sermon to the people. He said: “Your blood and your wealth are sacred to one another as the sanctity of this day, in this month, in this city. All matters of the days of ignorance are placed under my feet (i.e., they are no longer valid), and the blood feuds of the days of ignorance are abolished. The first blood I forgive from among our blood is that of Ibn Rabi’ah, who was being suckled among Banu Sa’d and was killed by Hudhayl (so I do not seek retribution for it). Likewise, the usury of the days of ignorance is all abolished (i.e., no one should take the accrued interest of that time), and the first usury I forgo from among our usury is that of Abbas bin Abdul Muttalib (may Allah be pleased with him), for it is all abolished. Fear Allah regarding women, for you have taken them by Allah’s trust and made their private parts lawful by Allah’s word (i.e., marriage). Your right over them is that they do not allow anyone you dislike to sit on your bedding (i.e., in your house). If they do so, then strike them in a way that does not cause injury (i.e., no bones broken, no organ lost, no disfigurement). Their right over you is that you provide for them food and clothing according to custom. I am leaving among you something that if you hold fast to it, you will never go astray: the Book of Allah. You will be asked about me (on the Day of Judgment), so what will you say?” They all said, “We bear witness that you have conveyed the message of Allah, fulfilled the trust of Prophethood, and advised the Ummah.” Then he (peace and blessings be upon him) raised his index finger towards the sky and pointed it towards the people and said, “O Allah, bear witness! O Allah, bear witness! O Allah, bear witness!” three times (and gestured thus). Then the call to prayer and the Iqamah were given, and he led the Zuhr prayer, then the Iqamah was given and he led the Asr prayer, and he did not pray anything between them (i.e., no Sunnah or Nafl). Then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) mounted and came to the place of standing (Mawqif), turned the belly of his she-camel towards the rocks, kept the path in front of him, faced the Qiblah, and remained there until sunset. The yellow color (of the sun) gradually faded, and the sun’s disc set. Then (he mounted), seated Sayyiduna Usamah (may Allah be pleased with him) behind him, and returned (towards Muzdalifah), and the reins of Qaswa were so tight that its head touched the saddle’s front (the place where a rider sometimes rests his foot when tired). He (peace and blessings be upon him) gestured with his right hand, “O people, go slowly and calmly,” and when he came to a sand hill (where the crowd was less), he loosened the reins a bit so the she-camel could climb. (Eventually, they reached Muzdalifah, and there he prayed Maghrib and Isha with one Adhan and two Iqamahs, and did not pray anything between the two obligatory prayers (i.e., no Sunnah, etc.). Then he (peace and blessings be upon him) lay down. (SubhanAllah, what devoted servants the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) had, who observed and preserved every act of his day and night, sleep and wakefulness, eating and drinking. May Allah have mercy on them.) When morning came and Fajr became apparent, he prayed Fajr with Adhan and Iqamah, then mounted Qaswa until he came to al-Mash’ar al-Haram, faced the Qiblah, supplicated to Allah, said Allahu Akbar, La ilaha illallah, and proclaimed His Oneness, and remained there until it became quite bright. He (peace and blessings be upon him) left there before sunrise, and seated Sayyiduna Fadl bin Abbas (may Allah be pleased with him) behind him. Fadl (may Allah be pleased with him) was a young, handsome, fair-skinned man with good hair. When he (peace and blessings be upon him) set out, a group of women was passing by, each riding on a camel, and all were moving along. Sayyiduna Fadl began to look at them, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) placed his hand on Fadl’s face (and did not say anything. SubhanAllah, what beautiful manners and how excellently he forbade evil). Fadl turned his face to the other side and began to look, so the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) again turned his hand and placed it on his face, so Fadl turned his face to the other side and looked again, until they reached Batn Muhassir. Then he made the she-camel go a little faster and took the middle path that leads to Jamrah al-Kubra, until he came to the Jamrah near the tree (which is called Jamrah Aqabah), and threw seven pebbles at it, saying Allahu Akbar with each pebble, pebbles that could be thrown with a pinch (and were the size of a chickpea), and he threw them standing in the middle of the valley (so that Mina, Arafat, and Muzdalifah were on his right and Makkah on his left). Then he came to the place of sacrifice and slaughtered sixty-three camels with his own blessed hand, and gave the rest to Sayyiduna Ali (may Allah be pleased with him) to slaughter. He included him in his sacrifice, and then ordered that a piece of meat be taken from each camel, placed in a pot, and cooked. Then he (peace and blessings be upon him) and Sayyiduna Ali (may Allah be pleased with him) both ate from it and drank its broth. Then he (peace and blessings be upon him) mounted and came to the House of Allah and performed the Tawaf of Ifadah and prayed Zuhr in Makkah. Then he came to the Banu Abdul Muttalib, who were giving water at Zamzam. He (peace and blessings be upon him) said, “Draw water, O children of Abdul Muttalib! If I did not fear that people would crowd you and prevent you from drawing water, I would have joined you in drawing water (i.e., if he (peace and blessings be upon him) had done so, it would have become Sunnah, and the whole Ummah would have started drawing water, and their privilege would have been lost).” Then they gave him a bucket, and he (peace and blessings be upon him) drank from it."
"708","`Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (may Allah be pleased with them both) says that` when we set out in the morning with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) from Mina towards Arafat, some of us were reciting the Talbiyah and some were proclaiming Takbir."
"709","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Muhammad bin Abi Bakr Thaqafi (may Allah be pleased with him) that he asked Sayyiduna Anas bin Malik (may Allah be pleased with him) while both of them were going from Mina to Arafat: ""What would you people do on this day with the Noble Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him)?"" Sayyiduna Anas (may Allah be pleased with him) said: ""If any of us said 'La ilaha illallah', no one would stop him, and if any of us said 'Allahu Akbar', no one would stop him either."
"710","Narrated from Umm al-Mu’minin Aisha Siddiqa (may Allah be pleased with her): She said that the Quraysh and those who followed the religion of the Quraysh used to stop at Muzdalifah and called themselves Hums. (Abu al-Haitham said that this is the name of the Quraysh and their descendants, and of Kinana and Jadila Qais, because they were strict and severe in their religion.) And the rest of the Arabs used to stop at Arafat. Then when Islam came, Allah Almighty commanded His Noble Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) to come to Arafat and stop there, and return from there. And this is the meaning of the verse: “Return from where all the people return.” __QUR_N__ __XREF_N__ __REF_N__"
"711","Jubair bin Mut’im (may Allah be pleased with him) said: My camel was lost, so I went out searching for it on the Day of Arafah. Then I saw that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) was standing in Arafat with the people. So I said, “By Allah, these are the people of Hums! How did they get here?” (That is, the Quraysh would not go beyond Muzdalifah.) And the Quraysh were counted among the Hums (those who would not go beyond Muzdalifah)."
"712","It is narrated from Kuraib that he asked Sayyiduna Usama bin Zaid (may Allah be pleased with him): When you were riding behind the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) on the evening of Arafah, what did you do? He said: We came to the valley where people make their camels kneel for the Maghrib prayer. The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) made his she-camel kneel, dismounted, and urinated. And Sayyiduna Usama (may Allah be pleased with him) did not mention the pouring of water. Then he asked for water for ablution and performed a light ablution, not complete (i.e., washed each limb once). I said: O Messenger of Allah! The prayer? He (peace and blessings be upon him) said: The prayer is ahead of you. Then he (peace and blessings be upon him) mounted until we reached Muzdalifah, and the call for Maghrib prayer was given, and the people made their camels kneel and did not untie them until the call for Isha was given, and he (peace and blessings be upon him) led the Isha prayer, then the camels were untied. I said: Then what did you do in the morning? He said: Then Sayyiduna Fadl bin Abbas (may Allah be pleased with him) rode behind him (peace and blessings be upon him), and I walked on foot with the first group of the Quraysh."
"713","It is narrated from 'Urwah that he said: Someone asked Sayyiduna Usamah bin Zaid (may Allah be pleased with him) in my presence (or he said that I myself asked Sayyiduna Usamah, may Allah be pleased with him), and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) had seated him on his camel at 'Arafat, that how did the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) proceed? (That is, at what pace did he make the camel walk?) So he said: He would proceed at a gentle (slow) pace, and then when he found an open space, that is, where the crowd was less, he would make it go a little faster."
"714","`Sayyiduna Ibn Umar (may Allah be pleased with them both) narrates that` the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) combined the Maghrib and Isha prayers at Muzdalifah and did not perform any (other) rak'ah between the two (prayers), and he performed three rak'ahs for Maghrib and two rak'ahs for Isha. And Sayyiduna Abdullah (may Allah be pleased with him) also continued to combine (Maghrib and Isha) in this manner until he met Allah, the Exalted."
"715","Sayyiduna Sa'id bin Jubair (may Allah be pleased with him) says that we returned to Muzdalifah with Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (may Allah be pleased with them both), and there he led us in Maghrib and Isha prayers with a single call to prayer (takbir). Then he returned and said that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) had led us in prayer at this very place in the same manner."
"716","`Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Mas'ud (may Allah be pleased with him) says that` I always saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) performing the prayer at its (prescribed) time except for two prayers. One was Maghrib and 'Isha, which he combined and performed at Muzdalifah, and (the second) was the Fajr prayer on its morning, which he performed before its (usual) time."
"717","Narrated from Umm al-Mu’minin Aisha Siddiqa (may Allah be pleased with her) that she said: Umm al-Mu’minin Sawda (may Allah be pleased with her) sought permission from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) on the night of Muzdalifah to return to Mina before him and to get ahead of the crowd, and she was a rather heavy (i.e., stout) woman. The narrator said that the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) granted her permission, so she departed before the return of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), and we stayed until we had performed the morning prayer and then returned with the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him). (Umm al-Mu’minin Aisha Siddiqa, may Allah be pleased with her, says:) If I had also sought permission from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) as Sawda (may Allah be pleased with her) did, and had left with his permission, it would have been good, and even better than that which made me happy."
"718","‘Abdullah, the freed slave of Lady Asma’ (may Allah be pleased with her), says: Lady Asma’ (may Allah be pleased with her) said to me while she was staying near Muzdalifah Dar, “Has the moon set?” I said, “No.” So she prayed for a short while, then said to me, “O my son! Has the moon set?” I said, “Yes.” She said, “Set out with me.” So we set out until she stoned the Jamrah, then she prayed at her place of stay. I said, “We have set out very early in the morning.” She said, “O my son! There is no harm, for the Noble Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) has permitted women to set out early in the morning.”"
"719","`Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both) says that` the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) sent me from Muzdalifah with the luggage (or he said: with the weak ones) during the night."
"720","It is narrated from Salim bin Abdullah that (his father) Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar, may Allah be pleased with them both, used to send the weak people who were with him ahead so that they could spend the night at Al-Mash'ar Al-Haram, which is in Muzdalifah, and remember Allah as long as they wished. Then they would return before the Imam's standing. So some of them would reach Mina at the time of the morning prayer and some after it. And Sayyiduna Ibn Umar, may Allah be pleased with them both, used to say that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, had permitted these weak people to do so."
"721","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both) that the Noble Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) seated Sayyiduna Fadl (bin Abbas) (may Allah be pleased with him) behind him on the camel from Muzdalifah. (The narrator) said that Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both) informed me, and he was informed by Sayyiduna Fadl (may Allah be pleased with him), that the Noble Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) continued to recite the Talbiyah until the stoning of Jamrah Aqabah."
"722","'It is narrated from Abdur Rahman bin Yazid that when Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Mas'ud (may Allah be pleased with them both) returned from Muzdalifah, he recited the Talbiyah. So the people said, ""Perhaps he is a man from the village?"" (i.e., who is now reciting the Talbiyah). Then Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Mas'ud (may Allah be pleased with them both) said, ""Have the people forgotten (i.e., the Sunnah of the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him) or gone astray? I myself heard from the one upon whom Surah Al-Baqarah was revealed (i.e., the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him) that he used to recite the Talbiyah at this place.""'"
"723","It is narrated from A’mash who says: I heard Hajjaj bin Yusuf saying in a sermon: Keep the same order of the Noble Qur’an as was set by Jibreel (peace be upon him). The surah in which Baqarah is mentioned should come first, then the surah in which Nisa is mentioned, then the surah in which Aal-e-Imran is mentioned. A’mash said: Then I met Ibrahim and informed him of this matter, so he criticized it and then said that Abdur Rahman bin Yazid narrated to me that he was with Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Mas’ud (may Allah be pleased with them both), and they came to Jamrah Aqabah and, standing in the valley with the Jamrah in front of them, threw seven pebbles at it from behind the stream, saying “Allahu Akbar” with each pebble. (The narrator) said: I said to him, “O Abu Abdur Rahman!” (this is the kunyah of Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Mas’ud, may Allah be pleased with them both), “People throw pebbles while standing above.” He replied, “By Him besides whom there is no deity, this is the place where Surah Al-Baqarah was revealed (i.e., the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, threw pebbles from here).”"
"724","Sayyiduna Jabir (may Allah be pleased with him) says: I saw the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) throwing pebbles at Jamrah Aqabah on the Day of Sacrifice from his camel, and he said: ""Learn your rites of Hajj from me, for I do not know whether I will perform Hajj after this year."
"725","`Sayyiduna Jabir bin Abdullah (may Allah be pleased with him) says that` I saw the Noble Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) throw at the Jamrah with pebbles that are thrown with the fingertips."
"726","`Sayyiduna Jabir bin Abdullah (may Allah be pleased with him) reports that` the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) stoned the Jamrah on the Day of Nahr at the time of forenoon, and on the following days after the sun had declined."
"727","‘Sayyiduna Jabir (may Allah be pleased with him) reports that’ the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: “Taking stones for istinja (purification) should be in odd numbers, and the pebbles for Jamrah are in odd numbers, and the Sa’i between Safa and Marwah is in odd numbers, and the Tawaf of the Ka’bah is in odd numbers (that is, all three are seven each), and it is necessary that whoever takes stones for istinja should take an odd number (that is, three or five, in which purification is properly achieved. That is, if purification is achieved with four, then take one more so that it becomes odd. And some foolish jurists who have written that at the time of purification, one should strike the stone three times so as to avoid using a tasbih, this is an innovation, baseless, and a futile act. And taking an odd number of stones is considered mustahabb (recommended) according to the majority of scholars).”"
"728","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Ibn Umar (may Allah be pleased with them both) that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) had his head shaved during the Farewell Pilgrimage."
"729","Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said, ""O Allah! Forgive those who shave their heads."" The people said, ""O Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him)! And those who trim their hair?"" Then he said, ""O Allah! Forgive those who shave their heads."" The people again said, ""O Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him)! And those who trim their hair (i.e., pray for their forgiveness as well)?"" He said, ""O Allah! Forgive those who shave their heads."" Again the people said, ""O Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him)! (Pray for the forgiveness of) those who trim their hair as well."" Then he (peace and blessings be upon him) said, ""And (forgive) those who trim their hair (as well)."
"730","Narrated from Sayyiduna Anas bin Malik (may Allah be pleased with him) that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) stoned the Jamrah ‘Aqabah, then came to the sacrificial camels and performed the sacrifice. And the barber was sitting, so he (peace be upon him) pointed with his hand towards his head. The barber then shaved the right side, and he (peace be upon him) distributed those hairs among the people who were near him. Then he said, ""Now shave the other side!"" Then he asked, ""Where is Abu Talhah (may Allah be pleased with him)?"" Then he gave those hairs to him."
"731","`Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Amr bin Al-As (may Allah be pleased with him) says that` the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) was standing while mounted on his she-camel and people began asking him questions about religious matters. So one person said, ""O Messenger of Allah (peace be upon him)! I did not know that stoning (Rami) should be done before sacrifice (Nahr), and I performed the sacrifice before stoning."" The Prophet (peace be upon him) said, ""There is no harm, now perform the stoning."" Another said, ""I did not know that sacrifice should be done before shaving the head, and I shaved my head before the sacrifice."" The Prophet (peace be upon him) said, ""Now perform the sacrifice, and there is no harm."" (The narrator) said, ""I heard that on that day, whoever asked the Prophet (peace be upon him) about any such act which a person forgets and does out of order, he (peace be upon him) replied, 'Now do it, and there is no harm.'"
"732","`Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Amr bin al-As (may Allah be pleased with him) says that` I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) while he was standing near Jamrah Aqabah, that a person came to the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and said, ""O Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him)! I shaved my head before throwing the pebbles."" So the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said, ""Now throw the pebbles, and there is no harm."" And another person came and said, ""I slaughtered (the sacrifice) before throwing (the pebbles)?"" So the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said, ""Now throw (the pebbles), and there is no harm."" And a third person came and said, ""I performed the Tawaf Ifadah of the House (Ka'bah) before throwing (the pebbles)?"" So the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said, ""Now throw (the pebbles), and there is no harm."" The narrator said that whatever was asked of the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) that day regarding something being done before or after (its proper time), the Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said, ""Now do it, and there is no harm."
"733","`Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them) says that` the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) offered the Zuhr prayer at Dhu’l-Hulayfah. Then he (peace and blessings be upon him) had his she-camel brought, and he performed Ish’ar on its right hump (i.e., made an incision with a spear or the like to let blood flow, as a sign of a sacrificial animal). Then he wiped that blood with his hand and hung two sandals around the neck of the she-camel. Then the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) mounted his ride. When it stood upright in the open field, the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) recited the Talbiyah for Hajj. (Talbiyah refers to saying “Labbayk Allahumma Labbayk.”)"
"734","It is narrated from ‘Amrah bint ‘Abdur Rahman that Ibn Ziyad wrote to Umm al-Mu’minin ‘A’ishah (may Allah be pleased with her) that Sayyiduna ‘Abdullah ibn ‘Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both) says: Whoever sends a sacrificial animal (as an offering) while staying at home without performing Hajj or ‘Umrah, then those things which are forbidden for a pilgrim become forbidden for him until the sacrifice is slaughtered. And I have sent a sacrificial animal, so please inform me of the ruling. Umm al-Mu’minin ‘A’ishah (may Allah be pleased with her) said: It is not as Ibn ‘Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both) has said. I myself have tied the garlands on the sacrificial animals of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him), and after placing them around their necks, he sent them with my father for sacrifice, and nothing became forbidden for the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) until they were slaughtered, which Allah had made lawful for him."
"735","Umm al-Mu'minin Aisha Siddiqa (may Allah be pleased with her) says that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) once sent goats to the House of Allah and put necklaces around their necks."
"736","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah, may Allah be pleased with him, that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, saw a man leading a sacrificial camel. He said, ""Ride on it."" The man replied, ""It is for sacrifice."" The Prophet, peace and blessings be upon him, said, ""Ride on it,"" and the second or third time he said, ""Woe to you."
"737","Abu Zubair says: I heard from Sayyiduna Jabir bin Abdullah (may Allah be pleased with him), and he was asked about riding the sacrificial animal. He said: When you are in need (and cannot find another ride), then ride it in such a way that you do not cause it harm."
"738","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both) that Dhu’ayb Abu Qubaysah (may Allah be pleased with him) reported from him that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) used to send sacrificial camels with him and would instruct that if any of them became tired and there was fear of its death, then it should be slaughtered, and its sandals should be dipped in its blood and marked on its hump, and neither you nor any of your companions should eat from it."
"739","`Sayyiduna Jabir bin Abdullah (may Allah be pleased with him) says that` we set out with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) having entered into the state of Ihram for Hajj, so he (peace be upon him) commanded us that seven of us should share in a camel or a cow."
"740","`Sayyiduna Jabir bin Abdullah (may Allah be pleased with him) reports that` the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) slaughtered a cow on behalf of Umm al-Mu'mineen Aisha Siddiqa (may Allah be pleased with her) on the day of sacrifice."
"741","It is narrated from Ziyad bin Jubair that Ibn Umar (may Allah be pleased with them both) saw a man making a camel sit down and slaughtering it. He said, ""Make it stand up, tie its leg, and then slaughter it. This is the Sunnah of your Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him)."
"742","Amir al-Mu'minin Sayyiduna Ali (may Allah be pleased with him) says that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) commanded me to stand by his sacrificial camels and to distribute their meat, skins, and coverings as charity, and not to give the butcher his wages from them. And Sayyiduna Ali (may Allah be pleased with him) said that we will pay the butcher's wages from our own resources."
"743","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Ibn Umar, may Allah be pleased with them both, that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, performed the Tawaf al-Ifadah on the day of sacrifice and then returned and offered the Zuhr prayer in Mina. Nafi' said that Sayyiduna Ibn Umar, may Allah be pleased with them both, used to perform the Tawaf al-Ifadah on the day of sacrifice, return, and offer the Zuhr prayer in Mina, and he used to say that the Noble Prophet, peace and blessings be upon him, did the same."
"744","It is narrated from Ibn Jurayj that ‘Ata informed him that Sayyiduna Ibn ‘Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both) used to give the verdict that whoever performed the Tawaf of the House (Ka‘bah) became halal (released from Ihram), whether he was a pilgrim (Haji) or not (i.e., one performing ‘Umrah). I asked ‘Ata, “From where did he derive this?” He said, “From this verse in which Allah Almighty said: ‘Then the place of sacrifice is at the Ancient House (Ka‘bah)’ { الحج : 33 } .” So I said, “But this is after coming from ‘Arafat.” He said, “The statement of Sayyiduna Ibn ‘Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both) is (that the place of release) is the House of Allah, whether it is after ‘Arafat or before it.” And he derived this from the blessed action of the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him), for he himself, during the Farewell Hajj, commanded the people to come out of Ihram."
"745","Narrated from Umm al-Mu'mineen Aisha Siddiqa (may Allah be pleased with her) that she became menstruating at (the place) Sarif and became pure at Arafah (i.e., performed ghusl for standing at Arafah), and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: ""The Tawaf of Safa and Marwah is sufficient for you for both Hajj and Umrah."
"746","Umm al-Mu’minin Aisha Siddiqa (may Allah be pleased with her) narrates that in the year of the Farewell Hajj, we set out (from Madinah) with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him). Some of us assumed ihram only for ‘Umrah, some assumed ihram for both Hajj and ‘Umrah, and some assumed ihram only for Hajj. And the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) himself assumed ihram only for Hajj. (Thus) whoever assumed ihram only for ‘Umrah became halal (came out of ihram) as soon as he performed tawaf, but those who assumed ihram for Hajj or for both Hajj and ‘Umrah did not become halal until the Day of Sacrifice (Yawm al-Nahr)."
"747","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Ibn Umar (may Allah be pleased with them both) that the Noble Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him), Sayyiduna Abu Bakr, and Sayyiduna Umar (may Allah be pleased with them both) used to stay at Abtah."
"748","‘Umm al-Mu’minin Aisha Siddiqa (may Allah be pleased with her) says that staying at Abtah (Muhassab) is not a (confirmed) Sunnah, and the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) only stayed there because it was easier to depart from there when he (peace be upon him) left (from Mina towards Makkah)."
"749","Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him) says: We were in Mina when the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said to us: Tomorrow we will camp at Khayf Bani Kinana, where the disbelievers swore an oath of disbelief. And that the Quraysh and Bani Kinana swore that they would neither marry with Bani Hashim and Bani Abdul Muttalib (i.e., their clans), nor buy or sell with them, until they handed over the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) to them. And what is meant by Khayf Bani Kinana is Muhassab."
"750","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Ibn Umar (may Allah be pleased with them) that Sayyiduna Abbas bin Abdul Muttalib (may Allah be pleased with him) sought permission from the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) to stay in Makkah during the nights of Mina because he was responsible for serving Zamzam water, so the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) granted him permission."
"751","Bakr bin Abdullah Muzani says: I was sitting near the Ka'bah with Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them) when a villager came and said, ""What is the reason that I see the children of your uncle serving honey drink and milk, while you serve date drink? Have you chosen this out of need or out of miserliness?"" Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them) replied, ""All praise is due to Allah! We are neither in need nor miserly. The real reason is that the Noble Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) once came on his she-camel, and Usamah (may Allah be pleased with him) was behind him. The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) asked for water, so we brought a bowl of date drink. The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) drank from it, and what remained he gave to Sayyiduna Usamah (may Allah be pleased with him) to drink, and the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said, 'You have done well, and do so always.' Therefore, what the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) has commanded, we do not wish to change."
"752","'Abdur Rahman bin Humaid says: I heard Umar bin Abdul Aziz saying to the people sitting in his gathering, ""What have you heard about residing in Makkah?"" So Saib bin Yazid said: I heard Alaa (may Allah be pleased with him) (or he said: Alaa bin Hadrami, may Allah be pleased with him) say that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: The emigrant, after performing the rites of Hajj, should stay in Makkah for three days (meaning, he should not stay more than this). (For those who migrated from Makkah, it was forbidden to reside in Makkah or make it their homeland after migration. However, after Hajj and Umrah, a permission of three days is given in this hadith.)"
"753","`Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both) says that` people were moving here and there when the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said that no person should depart until he has performed the Tawaf of the Ka'bah at the time of leaving."
"754","‘Umm al-Mu’minin Aisha Siddiqa (may Allah be pleased with her) says that Umm al-Mu’minin Safiyyah bint Huyayy (may Allah be pleased with her) experienced menstruation after performing the Tawaf al-Ifadah. So I mentioned this to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him). He (peace and blessings be upon him) said: “Will she (Umm al-Mu’minin Safiyyah, may Allah be pleased with her) detain us in Makkah?” Umm al-Mu’minin Aisha (may Allah be pleased with her) said: “O Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him)! She has already performed the Tawaf al-Ifadah, and then menstruated afterwards.” So the Noble Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: “Then she may return (with us).”"
"755","`Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both) says that` people were commanded to depart last from near the House of Allah (i.e., after performing Tawaf), and there was a concession for menstruating women (i.e., regarding the Farewell Tawaf)."
"756","´Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both) says that` in the days of ignorance (that is, before Islam), people considered performing Umrah during the days of Hajj to be the greatest sin on earth, and they used to make the month of Muharram into Safar. } The reason was that three consecutive months are sacred months: Dhu al-Qa'dah, Dhu al-Hijjah, and Muharram. So they would become anxious and could not commit robbery, because even the polytheists of Makkah respected the sacred months. (It is unfortunate that today Muslims do not even know which months are sacred, let alone respect them.) Therefore, they invented this mischief that instead of Muharram, they would write Safar and would commit much robbery, and when the month of Safar came, they would honor it like Muharram. And this was the ""Nasi"" which Allah Almighty mentions as the habit of the polytheists in the Qur'an. { They used to say that when the backs of the camels become good (that is, the wounds caused by the journey of Hajj have healed), and the tracks of the pilgrims' camels have disappeared from the roads, and the month of Safar is over, then it is permissible for the one performing Umrah to do Umrah. Then, when the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) and his companions entered Makkah in the state of Ihram on the fourth of Dhu al-Hijjah, he (peace and blessings be upon him) commanded them to convert the Ihram of Hajj into Umrah (as is the view of Ibn Qayyim and others). So this seemed very strange to the people, and they said, ""O Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him)! How should we become lawful? (That is, completely or partially, should we still avoid some things?)"" So he (peace and blessings be upon him) said, ""Become completely lawful (that is, there is no need to avoid anything)."
"757","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both) that the Noble Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said to a woman from among the Ansar, who was called Umm Sinan: ""Why do you not go with us for Hajj?"" She replied, ""My husband has only two camels; he and his son have gone for Hajj on one, and our servant brings water on the other."" So the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said, ""Umrah in Ramadan is equal to Hajj (or he said: equal to performing Hajj with us)."
"758","Abu Ishaq says: I asked Sayyiduna Zaid bin Arqam (may Allah be pleased with him), ""In how many battles did you participate with the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him)?"" He said, ""In seventeen battles."" And he narrated to me that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) fought nineteen battles and performed one Hajj after migration, which is called the Farewell Hajj. (The narrator of the hadith) Abu Ishaq said that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) performed another Hajj in Makkah (before migration)."
"759","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Anas (may Allah be pleased with him) that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) performed four ‘Umrahs, and apart from the one performed with Hajj, all were in the month of Dhu al-Qa‘dah. One ‘Umrah was from Hudaybiyyah or in the year of Hudaybiyyah in Dhu al-Qa‘dah, the second in Dhu al-Qa‘dah of the following year, the third ‘Umrah was from Ji‘ranah, where the spoils of the Battle of Hunayn were distributed, and that too was in Dhu al-Qa‘dah, and the fourth ‘Umrah was the one performed with Hajj."
"760","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both) that Sayyiduna Muawiyah bin Sufyan (may Allah be pleased with him) informed him. He said: I cut the hair of the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) on (the hill of) Marwah with the blade of an arrow. (Or he said: I saw the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) on Marwah having his hair cut with the blade of an arrow.)"
"761","Umm al-Mu'minin (Aisha Siddiqa) (may Allah be pleased with her) says: I said, ""O Messenger of Allah! People will return from Makkah with two acts of worship (that is, Hajj and 'Umrah separately), and I will return with only one act of worship."" So the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said, ""You stay; when you become pure, go to Tan'eem and proclaim the Talbiyah, and then meet us at such-and-such a place."" I think the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said, ""on the next day."" And the reward for your 'Umrah will be according to your hardship and expenditure."
"762","Narrated Abdullah bin Umar (may Allah be pleased with them) that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), when he would return from armies or from a small group of armies or from Hajj or Umrah, whenever he reached a hill or elevated stony ground, he would say ""Allahu Akbar"" three times, then he would say: ""There is no one worthy of worship except Allah alone, He has no partner, His is the dominion and to Him belongs all praise, and He has power over all things. We are returning, repenting, worshipping, prostrating, and praising our Lord specially. Allah has fulfilled His promise, helped His servant, and He alone defeated the armies (of the disbelievers)."
"763","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Umar (may Allah be pleased with them both) that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) made his camel sit on the stony ground of Dhul-Hulaifah and prayed there, and (Sayyiduna) Abdullah bin Umar (may Allah be pleased with them both) used to do the same."
"764","It is narrated from Nafi‘ that whenever Abdullah bin Umar (may Allah be pleased with them) returned from Hajj or ‘Umrah, he would make his camel sit on the stony ground of Dhu’l-Hulayfah where the Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) had made his camel sit."
"765","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Ibn Umar (may Allah be pleased with them both) that the Noble Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) used to rest at the end of the night in the valley of Dhul-Hulaifah, in the bottom of the valley. Then the Prophet’s (peace and blessings be upon him) companion (an angel) came and it was said to him that he (peace and blessings be upon him) was in the blessed plain (Bathaa’). Musa, the narrator, says that Salim made our mount sit at the place where Sayyiduna Abdullah Ibn Umar (may Allah be pleased with them both) used to make his mount sit, and he used to search for the place where the Noble Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) spent the night. That place is below the mosque which is built in the lower part of the valley, and the place is between the mosque and the qiblah."
"766","`Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that` when Allah Almighty granted His Messenger (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) victory over Makkah, he (peace be upon him) stood among the people and praised and glorified Allah Almighty, then said: Allah Almighty prevented the people of the Elephant from entering Makkah, and He gave authority over it to His Messenger (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) and the believers. And before me, fighting in it was not made lawful for anyone, and it was made lawful for me only for a short period of the day. And after me, it will never be lawful for anyone. Then its game should not be chased, its thorn should not be broken, its lost property should not be picked up except by one who announces it so that it may be returned to its owner. And if someone is killed, his heir has two options: either to accept blood money (compensation) or to have the killer executed in retribution. Sayyiduna Abbas (may Allah be pleased with him) submitted: O Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him), except for Idhkhir (a type of grass), do not make it unlawful, for we use it in our graves and houses (it is used in roofing). The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Fine, Idhkhir (the grass) is allowed, you may cut it. Then a man from Yemen named Abu Shah stood up and said: O Messenger of Allah! Write it down for me. The Prophet (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Write it down for Abu Shah. Walid said: I asked Awza'i what is meant by ""O Messenger of Allah! Write it down for me."" He said: This very sermon which the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) delivered (i.e., Abu Shah had it written down because it was a matter of great benefit)."
"767","`Sayyiduna Jabir (may Allah be pleased with him) says that` I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) say, ""It is not lawful for anyone to carry weapons in Makkah."
"768","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Jabir bin Abdullah Ansari, may Allah be pleased with him, that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, entered Makkah (Qutaiba said: entered on the day of the conquest of Makkah) and he, peace and blessings be upon him, was wearing a black turban (and he, peace and blessings be upon him,) entered without Ihram."
"769","Narrated from Sayyiduna Anas bin Malik (may Allah be pleased with him): In the year Makkah was conquered, the Noble Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) entered Makkah wearing a helmet on his head. Then when he removed the helmet, a man came and said that Ibn Khatal is clinging to the curtains of the Ka'bah (hiding). So the Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said: Kill him."
"770","Umm al-Mu’minin Aisha Siddiqa (may Allah be pleased with her) says: I asked the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him), “Is the wall of Hatim included in the House of Allah (Ka’bah)?” He (peace and blessings be upon him) replied, “Yes.” (From this, the school of Imam Abu Hanifa is refuted and performing Tawaf inside the Hatim is not permissible because it is part of the House of Allah.) I (then) asked, “Why did they not include it in the House of Allah?” He (peace and blessings be upon him) replied, “Your people ran short of funds.” (Then) I asked, “Why is its door so high?” He (peace and blessings be upon him) replied, “This too was done by your people so that they could allow whomever they wished to enter it and prevent whomever they wished from entering. And if your people had not recently left ignorance and if I did not fear that they would dislike it, I would have intended to include the walls of Hatim within the House of Allah and to bring its door down to the ground.”"
"771","‘Ata says that when, during the reign of Yazid bin Muawiyah, the Ka’bah was burned in the fighting with the people of Syria and whatever happened to it happened, Ibn Zubair (may Allah be pleased with him) left the Ka’bah as it was until people gathered for the Hajj season. Ibn Zubair (may Allah be pleased with him) intended to show the people the House of Allah and thereby encourage them to fight the people of Syria or prepare them for battle against the Syrians. Then, when the people were about to leave, he said, “O people! Advise me regarding the House of Allah: should I demolish it and rebuild it anew, or should I repair only the part that has been damaged?” Ibn Abbas (may Allah be pleased with them both) said, “I have an opinion, and it is that you should only repair what has been damaged among it and leave the Ka’bah as it was at the beginning of Islam, and leave those stones upon which people became Muslim and upon which the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) was sent.” Ibn Zubair (may Allah be pleased with him) said, “If any of you had his house burned, his heart would never be content until he rebuilt it anew. Then what about the House of your Lord, which is far superior? What should be done about it? I will seek guidance from my Lord three times, then I will make a firm decision about my action.” Then, after seeking guidance (Istikhara) three times, he decided to demolish and rebuild the Ka’bah. People became fearful, lest the first person to climb atop the Ka’bah to demolish it would be struck by a calamity from the sky (from this it is understood that the Owner of this House is above, and this was the belief of all the Companions). Until a man climbed up and removed a stone from it. When the people saw that no calamity befell him, they began to climb over one another and demolished the sacred House down to the ground. Ibn Zubair (may Allah be pleased with him) then erected a few pillars and hung curtains over them (so that people would continue to pray in the direction of the curtain and know the location of the Ka’bah, and those curtains remained) until the walls were raised high. Ibn Zubair (may Allah be pleased with him) said, “I heard from Umm al-Mu’minin Aisha Siddiqa (may Allah be pleased with her) that she said: The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) said, ‘If the people had not recently left disbelief, and if I had enough resources to rebuild it, I would have included five cubits of the Hatim within the Ka’bah, and I would have made a door through which people could enter and another through which they could exit.’” Then Ibn Zubair (may Allah be pleased with him) said, “Today we have enough resources to spend on it, and there is no fear from the people.” The narrator said: Then Ibn Zubair (may Allah be pleased with him) increased the wall by five cubits on the side of the Hatim until a foundation appeared there which people saw clearly (and that foundation was the foundation of Ibrahim, peace be upon him). Then he began to raise the wall from that foundation, and the length of the Ka’bah was eighteen cubits. When he increased it, it began to look small (meaning its width became greater and its length appeared less), so he increased its length by ten cubits as well, and he made two doors for it: one for entering and one for exiting. Then, when Abdullah bin Zubair (may Allah be pleased with him) was martyred, Hajjaj wrote to Abdul Malik bin Marwan informing him that the foundation laid by Ibn Zubair (may Allah be pleased with him) was upon the same foundations which the trustworthy people of Makkah had seen (i.e., the foundation of Ibrahim, peace be upon him). Abdul Malik wrote back to him, “We have no concern with the changes made by Ibn Zubair (may Allah be pleased with him). (Do this:) Leave what he increased in length, but remove what he added on the side of the Hatim and restore it to its original state, and close the door which he opened additionally.” Thus, Hajjaj demolished it and rebuilt it upon its original foundation."
"772","Abu Qaz'ah narrates that Abdul Malik bin Marwan was performing Tawaf of the House of Allah, and he said: ""May Allah destroy Ibn Zubair (may Allah be pleased with him), for he used to fabricate lies against Umm al-Mu'mineen Aisha Siddiqa (may Allah be pleased with her), and he used to say that he heard her say that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: 'O Aisha! If your people had not recently abandoned disbelief, I would have demolished the Ka'bah and included the Hijr (Hatim) within it, because your people have left out a portion of the Ka'bah's structure.'"" (Upon hearing this) Harith said: ""O Commander of the Faithful! Do not say so, for I too heard Umm al-Mu'mineen (may Allah be pleased with her) narrate this hadith."" So Abdul Malik said: ""If I had heard this hadith before demolishing the Ka'bah, I would have maintained the foundation of Ibn Zubair (may Allah be pleased with him)."
"773","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Abdullah bin Zaid bin Asim (may Allah be pleased with him) that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: Sayyiduna Ibrahim (peace be upon him) declared Makkah as a sanctuary (i.e., he made its sanctity apparent, otherwise its sanctity was from the day the heavens and the earth were created) and prayed for its people, and I declare Madinah as a sanctuary just as Ibrahim (peace be upon him) declared Makkah as a sanctuary, and I have prayed for the sa’ and mudd of Madinah, double what Ibrahim (peace be upon him) prayed for the people of Makkah."
"774","The conqueror of Persia, Sayyiduna Sa’d bin Abi Waqqas (may Allah be pleased with him), says that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: I declare the area between the two black stones as a sanctuary (Haram), so that no thorny tree should be cut there, nor should any game be hunted there. And he said: Madinah is better for them, if only they understood (this address is to those who leave Madinah for other places, or to all Muslims). And no one turns away from residing in Madinah out of aversion except that Allah brings someone better than him to it. And no one endures its hunger, thirst, and hardship with patience except that I will be his intercessor or witness on the Day of Resurrection."
"775","'Amir bin Sa'd narrates that Sayyiduna Sa'd (may Allah be pleased with him) went to his house which was in 'Aqiq, and (on the way) he saw a slave who was cutting a tree or plucking its leaves, so he seized his belongings. When Sayyiduna Sa'd returned, the family of that slave came and said, ""Please return it to him or grant it to us."" He replied, ""I seek refuge with Allah from returning something which the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) has granted to me as a gift."" And he refused to return his belongings."
"776","Sayyiduna Anas bin Malik (may Allah be pleased with him) narrates that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: O Allah! Grant Madinah twice the blessings as You have granted to Makkah."
"777","Ibrahim Taimi narrates from his father that he said: Ali bin Abi Talib (may Allah be pleased with him) delivered a sermon to us and said: Whoever claims that we (i.e., the Ahl al-Bayt) have anything other than the Book of Allah and this scroll— the narrator said the scroll was hanging from the sheath of his sword— then he has lied. And in this scroll, there is mention of the ages of camels (regarding zakat) and some details about wounds (i.e., regarding retribution and blood money). And in this scroll, it is also written that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: The area of Madinah between Mount ‘Ayr and Mount Thawr is a sanctuary (Haram). So whoever introduces a new thing (i.e., an innovation) in Madinah or gives shelter to an innovator, upon him is the curse of Allah, the angels, and all people. Allah will not accept any obligatory or voluntary act from him. And the protection given by any Muslim is equal; even the protection given by the lowest Muslim is to be honored. And whoever attributes himself to anyone other than his father, or claims to be the slave of anyone other than his masters, upon him is the curse of Allah, the angels, and all people, and Allah will not accept any obligatory or voluntary act from him on the Day of Resurrection. (* Here, “hadath” refers to any crime, and this (i.e., innovation) is also included in it.)"
"778","Narrated from Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) that when the first fruit would come to the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him), he would supplicate: ""O Allah! Bestow blessings upon our city, upon our fruits, upon our Madinah, and upon our mudd and sa’ (measures)."" Then he would give that fruit to the youngest child present in the gathering."
"779","Abu Sa'id Mawla Mahri narrates that he came to Sayyiduna Abu Sa'id Khudri (may Allah be pleased with him) during the nights of Harrah (that is, during the days when a famous turmoil occurred in Madinah Tayyibah and the oppressors looted Madinah) and consulted him about leaving Madinah for somewhere else. He complained to him about the high prices (inflation) and the large number of dependents, and informed him that he could not bear the hardship and hunger of Madinah. So Sayyiduna Abu Sa'id Khudri (may Allah be pleased with him) said, ""Woe to you! I will not advise you to do this (because) I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) say: 'No person endures the hardships here and then dies, except that I will be his intercessor or witness on the Day of Resurrection, if he is a Muslim.'"
"780","‘Mother of the Believers, Aisha Siddiqa (may Allah be pleased with her) says that when we came to Madinah (after migrating), there was an epidemic fever spreading there. And Abu Bakr (may Allah be pleased with him) and Bilal (may Allah be pleased with him) became ill. Then when the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) saw the illness of his companions, he prayed: O Allah! Make our Madinah beloved to us as You made Makkah beloved, or even more so, and make it a place of health, and bless us in its “Sa’” and “Mudd” (measures), and turn its fever towards Juhfa."
"781","Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him) reports that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: Angels are appointed at the entrances of Madinah; neither plague nor Dajjal can enter it."
"782","Narrated from Sayyiduna Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him) that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) said: A time will come upon the people when a man will call his nephew and his close relative, saying, ""Come to prosperity, come to prosperity,"" although Medina will be better for them if they only knew. And by the One in Whose hand is my soul, no one leaves Medina out of aversion to it except that Allah brings someone better than him to reside in Medina. Be aware that Medina is like a blacksmith's furnace; it removes impurities. And the Hour will not be established until Medina expels its wicked people just as a furnace removes the impurities of iron."
"783","Sayyiduna Jabir bin Samurah (may Allah be pleased with him) says: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say that Allah, the Glorious and Exalted, has named Madinah as ""Tābah"" (Tayyibah)."
"784","`Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) reports that` the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: Whoever intends evil against the people of this city (i.e., Madinah), Allah will dissolve him as salt dissolves in water."
"785","Sufyan bin Abi Zuhair (may Allah be pleased with him) says: I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: ""When Yemen is conquered, some people will drive their camels out of Madinah along with their families and servants, even though Madinah would be better for them, if only they knew. Then Syria will be conquered, and a group of people from Madinah will drive their camels out with their families and servants, and Madinah would be better for them, if only they knew. Then Iraq will be conquered, and a group of people from Madinah will drive their camels out with their families and servants, even though Madinah would be better for them, if only they knew."
"786","´Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah (may Allah be pleased with him) says that` I heard the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) say: People will leave Madinah despite its goodness, and none will remain in it except wild animals and birds. Then two shepherds from the tribe of Muzaynah will set out towards Madinah, calling their sheep, intending to go there, and they will find Madinah deserted. When they reach Thaniyyat al-Wada', they will fall down on their faces."
"787","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Abu Hurairah, may Allah be pleased with him, that the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings be upon him, said: Between my house and my pulpit is one of the gardens of Paradise, and my pulpit is upon my cistern."
"788","Anas bin Malik (may Allah be pleased with him) reports that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) looked towards Uhud (mountain) and said: ""Uhud is a mountain that loves us and we love it."
"789","Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him) reports that the Prophet Muhammad (peace and blessings be upon him) said: ""Mounts should not be saddled (i.e., journeys should not be undertaken) except towards three mosques: this mosque of mine (i.e., the mosque in Madinah, Masjid al-Nabawi), Masjid al-Haram, and Masjid al-Aqsa (i.e., Bayt al-Maqdis)."
"790","Abu Huraira (may Allah be pleased with him) reports that the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) said: Offering one prayer in this mosque of mine (the Prophet’s Mosque) is better than offering a thousand prayers in other mosques, except for Al-Masjid Al-Haram."
"791","Abu Salamah bin Abdur Rahman says: Abdur Rahman bin Abu Sa'id Al-Khudri (may Allah be pleased with him) passed by me, so I said to him: How did you hear your father (Sayyiduna Abu Sa'id Al-Khudri, may Allah be pleased with him) regarding what he used to say about this mosque whose foundation was laid on piety? He said: My father (may Allah be pleased with him) said: I entered upon the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) in the house of one of his wives and I asked: O Messenger of Allah! Which is the mosque about which Allah Almighty says its foundation was laid on piety? He (the narrator) says: The Prophet (peace and blessings be upon him) took a handful of pebbles and struck them on the ground and said: It is this mosque of yours in Madinah. (Abu Salamah bin Abdur Rahman says:) I also testify that I too heard your father (may Allah be pleased with him) mentioning it in the same way about this mosque."
"792","`Sayyiduna Ibn Umar (may Allah be pleased with them) narrates that` the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings be upon him) used to come to the Quba Mosque both on foot and riding, and he would offer two rak‘ahs of prayer there."
"793","It is narrated from Sayyiduna Ibn Umar (may Allah be pleased with them both) that he (Ibn Umar) used to come to (the mosque of) Quba every Saturday and used to say that I have seen the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) going to Quba every Saturday."
